---
import LegalLayout from '../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { PRIVACY_PATH, REFUNDS_PATH, SITE_BRAND, TERMS_PATH } from '../../lib/seo';
---

<LegalLayout
	title="Content License"
	description="iStockVisual license: free commercial and personal use of library images, with attribution required."
	heading="Content License"
	lede="Library images are free for commercial and personal use. Attribution is required on every size, including Pro downloads."
>
	<h2>1. What this license covers</h2>
	<p>
		This license applies to photos, illustrations, vectors, and other visual assets published in the
		iStockVisual library (“Library Content”). Most Library Content is generated or prepared for
		publication on {SITE_BRAND}. It is not public domain, and downloading a file does not transfer
		copyright to you.
	</p>
	<p>
		512 and 1K preview sizes are free. 2K, 4K, and 8K files require an active Pro plan or pass. The
		same license terms apply to every size and format (JPG, PNG, WEBP, and SVG).
	</p>

	<h2>2. What you may do</h2>
	<p>Subject to this license and our <a href={TERMS_PATH}>Terms of Use</a>, you may:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>Use Library Content in personal and commercial projects, including websites, ads, social posts, presentations, packaging, and print</li>
		<li>Edit, crop, color-grade, composite, and combine Library Content with your own work</li>
		<li>Use Library Content in client work, provided the client also follows this license</li>
		<li>Keep files you already downloaded if a plan later ends, still subject to this license</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>3. Attribution</h2>
	<p>
		You must credit the source whenever Library Content is used in a context where a credit can
		reasonably appear (websites, videos, print, apps, and similar). Use wording equivalent to:
	</p>
	<p><strong>Generated by {SITE_BRAND}</strong></p>
	<p>
		A link to the image page or to {SITE_BRAND} is preferred when the medium allows it. Each asset
		page includes copy-ready credit formats. Do not remove or obscure an existing credit on an
		unmodified file you redistribute as part of a larger work.
	</p>

	<h2>4. What you may not do</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Sell, license, or redistribute the original or lightly modified file as a standalone stock asset, template pack, or competing library item</li>
		<li>Claim exclusive ownership of unmodified Library Content, or register it as your trademark or copyright</li>
		<li>Use Library Content to imply that iStockVisual endorses a person, product, or cause</li>
		<li>Use Library Content in unlawful, deceptive, or hateful material</li>
		<li>Scrape, bulk-harvest, or automate downloads beyond ordinary personal or studio use, including after the fair-use cap described on the pricing page</li>
		<li>Share Pro login details so others can download HD files on your account</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>5. Browser tools and your own files</h2>
	<p>
		Image editor, convert, vectorize, social resize, watermark, and palette tools run in your
		browser. Files you choose on your device for those tools are not uploaded to iStockVisual and
		remain yours. If you start from Library Content, this license and the attribution requirement
		still apply to that content and to recognizable derivatives of it.
	</p>
	<p>
		Visual search may upload a query photo so we can match colors in the library. That upload is
		handled under the <a href={PRIVACY_PATH}>Privacy Policy</a> and is not added to the public
		library.
	</p>

	<h2>6. Trademarks and people</h2>
	<p>
		Library Content is produced for general creative use. It may depict objects, settings, or
		stylized scenes. You are responsible for any extra clearance your project needs (for example
		real trademarks, logos, or identifiable people that you add yourself).
	</p>

	<h2>7. Fair use, refunds, and changes</h2>
	<p>
		Download speed limits on HD files do not change this license. Refunds are described in the
		<a href={REFUNDS_PATH}>Refund Policy</a>. We may update this license; the version on this page
		applies to new downloads from the date it is posted. Files you already downloaded remain usable
		under the license that applied when you downloaded them, unless we must restrict use to comply
		with law.
	</p>
</LegalLayout>
